ively tested.\n  * The code runs both with CPU and Metal backends. With Metal is faster.\n\nDownload the GGUF from: https://huggingface.co/antirez/deepseek-v4-gguf\n\nThen to test it run with (but for production you may want to tune context, disable thinking for faster replies and so forth):\n    \n    `llama-cli \\\n        -m DeepSeek-V4-Flash-IQ2XXS-w2Q2K-AProjQ8-SExpQ8-OutQ8-chat.gguf \\\n        -cnv\n    `\n\n## About\n\nExperimental implementation of DeepSeek v4 flaash in llama.cpp\n\n### Resources\n\nReadme\n\nMIT license\n\n### Contributing\n\nContributing\n\n### Security policy\n\nSecurity policy\n\nActivity\n\n### Stars\n\n346 stars\n\n### Watchers\n\n8 watching\n\n### Forks\n\n65 forks--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF · Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF?local-app=llama.cpp)\nciteturn22search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; How to use ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF with llama.cpp:\n\n# \n\nggml-org\n\n/\n\nDeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF\n\nLike [Button: 25]\n\nFollow\n\nImage ggml-org [Button: 3.08k]\n\nText Generation GGUF quantized conversational\n\nLicense: mit\n\nModel card Files xet Community 2\n\n### Instructions to use ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n\n  * Notebooks\n  * Google Colab\n  * Kaggle\n  * Local Apps Settings\n  * llama.cpp\n\nHow to use ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF with llama.cpp:\n\n##### Install (macOS, Linux)\n    \n    curl -LsSf https://llama.app/install.sh | sh\n    # Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n    llama serve -hf ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF:MXFP4\n    # Run inference directly in the terminal:\n    llama cli -hf ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF:MXFP4\n\n##### Install from WinGet (Windows)\n    \n    winget install llama.cpp\n    # Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n    llama serve -hf ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF:MXFP4\n    # Run inference directly in the terminal:\n    llama cli -hf ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF:MXFP4\n\n##### Use pre-built binary\n    \n    # Download pre-built binary from:\n    # https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp/releases\n    # Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n    ./llama-server -hf ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF:MXFP4\n    # Run inference directly in the terminal:\n    ./llama-cli -hf ggml-org/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-0731-GGUF:MXFP4\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nteamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF · Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF?local-app=llama.cpp)\nciteturn22search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; How to use teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF with llama.cpp: ... GGUF quantizations of `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash` for use with the V4-aware llama.cpp fork at `cchuter/llama.cpp` @ `feat/v4-port-cuda`.\n\n# \n\nteamblobfish\n\n/\n\nDeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF\n\nLike [Button: 29]\n\nFollow\n\nImage Team Blobfish [Button: 16]\n\nText Generation GGUF llama.cpp deepseek-v4 Mixture of Experts imatrix conversational\n\nLicense: mit\n\nModel card Files xet Community 6\n\nDeploy\n\nCopy to bucket new\n\nUse this model\n\n### Instructions to use teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF with libraries, inference providers, notebooks, and local apps. Follow these links to get started.\n\nHow to use teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF with llama.cpp:\n\n##### Install (macOS, Linux)\n    \n    curl -LsSf https://llama.app/install.sh | sh\n    # Start a local OpenAI-compatible server with a web UI:\n    llama serve -hf teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF:Q4_K_M\n    # Run inference directly in the terminal:\n    llama cli -hf teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF:Q4_K_M\n\n##### Install from WinGet (Windows)\n    \n# DeepSeek V4 Flash · GGUF\n\nGGUF quantizations of `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash` for use with the V4-aware llama.cpp fork at `cchuter/llama.cpp` @ `feat/v4-port-cuda`.\n\n> 📦 Required: V4-aware llama.cpp fork. These quants don't load on upstream `ggml-org/llama.cpp` — V4 architecture support (compressor decode, hyperconnection, lightning indexer, FP8 KV simulation, NextN heads) lives only in the fork:\n>     \n>     `git clone -b feat/v4-port-cuda https://github.com/cchuter/llama.cpp\n>     `\n> \n> Full build + run instructions in Loading below.\n\n## Available quants\n\nQuant  | Size  | BPW  | Decode (M3 Ultra)  | gate-tools  | Notes\n--- | --- | --- | --- | --- | ---\nQ8_0  | ~282 GiB (7 shards)  | 8.50  | 21.69 t/s  | ✓ pass  | Reference. Full-fidelity baseline.\nQ4_K_M-XL  | ~163 GiB (4 shards)  | 4.92  | 22.85 t/s  | ✓ pass  | Recommended. K-quant body, non-expert tensors and embedding/output pinned at Q8_0. Matches Q8 on tool calling at half the size.\nQ2_K-XL  | ~100 GiB (3 shards)  | 3.01  | 23.38 t/s  | ✓ pass  | Smaller-footprint K-quant alternative to Q4_K_M-XL with the same XL pin recipe.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndeepseek-v4.1-flash (https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v4.1-flash)\nciteturn22search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday;     ollama run deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud\n\n82.9K 1 month ago\n\n## DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash is an advanced tool designed to enhance search capabilities, providing users with faster and more accurate results.\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash is an advanced tool designed to enhance search capabilities, providing users with faster and more accurate results.\n\nvision tools thinking cloud\n\nCost /1M tokens\n\n[Button: Peak] [Button: Off-Peak]\n\n$0.30\n\ninput\n\n$0.006\n\ncached\n\n$1.20\n\noutput\n\nContext\n\n1M tokens\n\nSize\n\n763B parameters\n    \n    ollama run deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud\n    \n    curl https://ollama.com/api/chat \\\n      -H \"Authorization: Bearer $OLLAMA_API_KEY\" \\\n      -d '{\n        \"model\": \"deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\n        \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}]\n      }'\n    \n    import os\n    from ollama import Client\n    \n    client = Client(\n        host='https://ollama.com',\n        headers={'Authorization': 'Bearer ' + os.environ['OLLAMA_API_KEY']},\n    )\n    \n    response = client.chat(\n        model='deepseek-v4.1-flash',\n        messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hello!'}],\n    )\n    print(response.message.content)\n    \n    import { Ollama } from 'ollama'\n    \n    const ollama = new Ollama({\n      host: 'https://ollama.com',\n      headers: { Authorization: 'Bearer ' + process.env.OLLAMA_API_KEY },\n    })\n    \n    const response = await ollama.chat({\n      model: 'deepseek-v4.1-flash',\n      messages: [{role: 'user', content: 'Hello!'}],\n    })\n    console.log(response.message.content)\n\n## Applications\n\nImage: Claude Code\n\nClaude Code `ollama launch claude --model deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud`\n\nImage: OpenCode\n\nOpenCode `ollama launch opencode --model deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud`\n\nImage: Hermes Agent\n\nHermes Agent `ollama launch hermes --model deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud`\n\nImage: OpenClaw\n\nOpenClaw `ollama launch openclaw --model deepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud`\n\n1 model\n\ndeepseek-v4.1-flash:cloud - · 1M context window · Text, Image · 1 month ago\n\n## Readme\n\nImage\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash: Pushing the Limits of KV Cache Compression\n\nDeepSeek-V4.1-Flash is an advanced tool designed to enhance search capabilities, providing users with faster and more accurate results. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nREADME.md · teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF at 8224b059b3bd5f5846538a804298412cc971ace3 (https://huggingface.co/teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF/blob/8224b059b3bd5f5846538a804298412cc971ace3/README.md?code=true)\nciteturn22search5 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago;  | GGUF quantizations of [`deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash`](https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash) for use with the V4-aware llama.cpp fork at [`cchuter/llama.cpp` @ `feat/v4-port`](https://github.com/cchuter/llama.cpp/tree/feat/v4-port). ... That makes the choice of dequant codepath matter as much as the bit-count: Q8_0's int8 × per-block-scale unpack is dramatically simpler than Q4_K_M's super-block path, so on this hardware **Q8_0 actually decoded faster than vanilla Q4_K_M** in our earlier benchmarks ([write-up](https://blog.teamblobfish.com/posts/deepseek-v4-flash-llama-cpp/)).\n\n8224b05\n\nDeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF / README.md\n\nImage: cchuter's picture\n\ncchuter\n\nREADME: explicit CUDA / non-Metal backends not supported (Metal-only ops)\n\n8224b05 verified\n\npreview code\n\n8.9 kB\n\n | ---\n | license: mit\n | base_model: deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash\n | tags:\n | - gguf\n | - llama.cpp\n | - deepseek-v4\n | - moe\n | pipeline_tag: text-generation\n | ---\n | \n | # DeepSeek V4 Flash · GGUF\n | \n | GGUF quantizations of [`deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash`](https://huggingface.co/deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash) for use with the V4-aware llama.cpp fork at [`cchuter/llama.cpp` @ `feat/v4-port`](https://github.com/cchuter/llama.cpp/tree/feat/v4-port).\n | \n | > ⚠️ These quants will **not** load on upstream `ggml-org/llama.cpp`. V4 architecture, V4-specific Metal kernels, and the f16 KV pin are only present in the fork above. Upstreaming is gated on the V3.2/DSA PR ([#21149](https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/pull/21149)) landing first.\n | \n | > 🖥️ **CUDA / NVIDIA / ROCm GPUs are not supported.** V4's custom ops — `ggml_dsv4_rope_tail`, `ggml_dsv4_hc_split_sinkhorn`, `ggml_dsv4_hc_weighted_sum`, `ggml_dsv4_hc_expand`, `ggml_dsv4_fp8_kv_quantize` — have **Metal kernels only** in this fork. Loading a V4 GGUF on a CUDA / ROCm / Vulkan backend will fail at the first dsv4 op (no kernel registered) or silently fall back to a partial CPU path that produces wrong results. The supported backends are **Apple Silicon (Metal)** and **CPU**. CUDA/ROCm support would require porting the five ops above; that work has not been done in this fork.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nDeepSeek V4 Support (WIP) · ggml-org llama.cpp · Discussion #22376 · GitHub (https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp/discussions/22376)\nciteturn22search6 [wordlim: 200] Published: 5 months ago; Crawled: last week; @wuwenthink try https://github.com/nisparks/llama.cpp/tree/wip/deepseek-v4-support ...     llama_model_load: error loading model: llama_model_loader: failed to load model from /data/dsv4/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-native.gguf\n\n# DeepSeek V4 Support (WIP) #22376\n\nnisparks started this conversation in Show and tell\n\nDeepSeek V4 Support (WIP) #22376\n\nApr 26, 2026 · 6 comments · 23 replies\n\nDiscussion options\n\n## \n\nnisparks Apr 26, 2026\n\nSo want pretty deep into optimizing DeepSeek V4 on my experimental branch, before I realized it wasn't the upstream version. I went back and ported to the upstream base, but it performs a little slower than my experimental branch. I will share both. Here is the Work in Progress, based on the upstream version: https://github.com/nisparks/llama.cpp/tree/wip/deepseek-v4-support The experimental branch is still a work in progress and will share later. Uploaded the GGUF here: https://huggingface.co/nsparks/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-GGUF\n\n## Replies: 6 comments · 23 replies\n\n  * Oldest\n  * Newest\n  * Top\n\nComment options\n\n### \n\nnisparks Apr 26, 2026\n\nCreated a draft with no intentions of merging: #22378 Just so it is easy to see the diff.\n\n### \n\nwuwenthink Apr 26, 2026\n\ntecaprovn/deepseek-v4-flash-gguf cannot success ,do you have gguf model can be use? thanks\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\n18 replies\n\n[Input] [Input] [Input] Show 13 previous replies\n\nComment options\n\n#### \n\nwuwenthink Apr 26, 2026\n\n> @wuwenthink, ah, I renamed it, \"native\" was a bad name for it, so I had that changed.\n\nI wish I could not find a suitable branch, so I can't convert the model to GGUF locally.\n\nwuwenthink Apr 26, 2026\n\n> @nisparks I made a Q2-Q3 mixed GGUF to fit almost exact the VRAM size of RTX Pro 6000. When offloading MOE to CPU, I also got 15-17 t/s.\n\n你是怎么转换成功的？\n我这边切了分支也报错 = =\n\nAll reactions\n\nComment options\n\n#### \n\nnisparks Apr 26, 2026\n\n@wuwenthink try https://github.com/nisparks/llama.cpp/tree/wip/deepseek-v4-support\n\nAll reactions\n\nComment options\n\n#### \n\nnisparks Apr 26, 2026\n\nOr https://github.com/nisparks/llama.cpp/tree/experiment/deepseek-v4-gguf-convert\n\nAll reactions\n\nComment options\n\n#### \n\nwuwenthink Apr 26, 2026\n\n> Or https://github.com/nisparks/llama.cpp/tree/experiment/deepseek-v4-gguf-convert\n\nok\n\nlovedheart Apr 26, 2026\n\n@wuwenthink I can upload a bf16 gguf ...\n\nYou must be logged in to vote\n\nAll reactions\n\n1 reply\n\nComment options\n\n#### \n\nwuwenthink Apr 26, 2026\n\n> @wuwenthink I can upload a bf16 gguf ...\n\nbut i dont have enough mem = =\n\nFringe210 Apr 28, 2026\n\nhttps://github.com/Fringe210/llama.cpp-deepseek-v4-flash-cuda <-- it works (18tokens/sec on single RTX 6000 96 gb) . 100% Minimax+clina+vstudio so needs a lot of love. Maybe it helps.\n\nColumbusAI Apr 30, 2026\n\n> https://github.com/Fringe210/llama.cpp-deepseek-v4-flash-cuda <-- it works (18tokens/sec on single RTX 6000 96 gb) . 100% Minimax+clina+vstudio so needs a lot of love. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndeepseek-v4-flash (https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v4-flash)\nciteturn22search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last month;     ollama run deepseek-v4-flash:cloud\ndeepseek-v4-flash\n\n445.4K 1 month ago\n\n## DeepSeek-V4-Flash is the official release of DeepSeek-V4-Flash, built for efficient reasoning across a 1M-token context window, outperforming DeepSeek-V4-Pro (Preview).\n\nDeepSeek-V4-Flash is the official release of DeepSeek-V4-Flash, built for efficient reasoning across a 1M-token context window, outperforming DeepSeek-V4-Pro (Preview).\n\nCost /1M tokens\n\n[Button: Base] [Button: Peak]\n\n$0.22\n\ninput\n\n$0.007\n\ncached\n\n$0.66\n\noutput\n\nContext\n\n1M tokens\n\nSize\n\n304B parameters\n\n[Button: CLI] [Button: cURL] [Button: Python] [Button: JavaScript]\n    \n    ollama run deepseek-v4-flash:cloud\n    \n    curl http://localhost:11434/api/chat \\\n      -d '{\n        \"model\": \"deepseek-v4-flash:cloud\",\n        \"messages\": [{\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"Hello!\"}]\n      }'\n    \n    from ollama import chat\n    \n    response = chat(\n        model='deepseek-v4-flash:cloud',\n        messages=[{'role': 'user', 'content': 'Hello!'}],\n    )\n    print(response.message.content)\n    \n    import ollama from 'ollama'\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nnsparks/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-GGUF · Hugging Face (https://huggingface.co/nsparks/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-GGUF)\nciteturn22search8 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Native, 1:1 conversion of `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash` from the original safetensors into a single GGUF file that preserves the model's native low-precision weights: ... This GGUF requires a llama.cpp build with native `F8_E4M3_B128` and `MXFP4` support and the DeepSeek V4 Flash architecture.\n\n# DeepSeek-V4-Flash native FP4 / FP8 GGUF\n\nNative, 1:1 conversion of `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash` from the original safetensors into a single GGUF file that preserves the model's native low-precision weights:\n\n  * Dense weights: FP8 E4M3 (`F8_E4M3_B128`, 128-element blocks with one E8M0 scale)\n  * MoE expert weights: MXFP4 (`MXFP4`)\n\nThis file is not derived from a higher-precision intermediate; the FP4 and FP8 codes from the upstream checkpoint are written directly into the GGUF.\n\n## File\n\nFile  | Size  | Quant\n--- | --- | ---\n`DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-native.gguf`  | ~146 GB  | F8_E4M3 + MXFP4\n\n## Loading\n\nThis GGUF requires a llama.cpp build with native `F8_E4M3_B128` and `MXFP4` support and the DeepSeek V4 Flash architecture. Stock upstream `llama.cpp` cannot load this file.\n\nReference (WIP) build that can both produce and run this GGUF:\n\n> https://github.com/nisparks/llama.cpp/tree/wip/deepseek-v4-support\n\nThat branch adds:\n\n  * `GGML_TYPE_F8_E4M3_B128` (ggml type 42)\n  * `LLAMA_FTYPE_MOSTLY_F8_E4M3_MXFP4` (ftype 41, exposed as `F8_E4M3_MXFP4` / `moe-f8-e4m3-mxfp4`)\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndeepseek-v4-gguf/README.md at main · arishma108/deepseek-v4-gguf · GitHub (https://github.com/arishma108/deepseek-v4-gguf/blob/main/README.md)\nciteturn22search9 [wordlim: 200] Published: 9 months ago; Crawled: 2 days ago;     ./llama-cli -m ../model/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-IQ1_S-XL-00001-of-00002.gguf \\ ...   * llama.cpp community for GGUF format and V4 support\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nREADME.md · teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF at 240b7aa9c75c94059b0c81e6d587677b3b7bfa21 (https://huggingface.co/teamblobfish/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-GGUF/blob/240b7aa9c75c94059b0c81e6d587677b3b7bfa21/README.md)\nciteturn22search10 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; GGUF quantizations of `deepseek-ai/DeepSeek-V4-Flash` for use with the V4-aware llama.cpp fork at `cchuter/llama.cpp` @ `feat/v4-port-cuda`. ... These quants don't load on upstream `ggml-org/llama.cpp` — V4 architecture support (compressor decode, hyperconnection, lightning indexer, FP8 KV simulation, NextN heads) lives only in the fork:\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nREADME.md · nsparks/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-GGUF at main (https://huggingface.co/nsparks/DeepSeek-V4-Flash-FP4-FP8-GGUF/blob/main/README.md)\nciteturn22search11 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; This GGUF requires a llama.cpp build with native `F8_E4M3_B128` and `MXFP4` support and the DeepSeek V4 Flash architecture.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nmistral_llama_large (https://github.com/ggerganov/llama.cpp/files/15192723/mistral_llama_large-gpu.pdf)\nciteturn22search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.3 years ago; = 4.78 GiB (5.67 BPW) ... llama_new_context_with_model: flash_attn = 0 ... V (f16):\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndeepseek-v4.1-flash (https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v4.1-flash)\nciteturn22view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v4.1-flash\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 160\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nInternal Error ()\nciteturn22view1 [wordlim: 200] Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v4\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 1\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTags · deepseek-v3.2 (https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v3.2/tags)\nciteturn22view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 5 days ago; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://ollama.com/library/deepseek-v3.2/tags\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 24\n"
